WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.400
A birthday party from hell and the&nbsp;
most famous manhunt in history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.162
Critics thought these movies&nbsp;
were silver-screen gold. Did you?

00:00:08.316 --> 00:00:13.760
As the only film on this list with a perfect&nbsp;
Metascore of 100, "Boyhood" has a lot of hype&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.480
to live up to. Directed and written by Richard&nbsp;
Linklater, "Boyhood" was filmed over the course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:24.400
of an outstanding 12 years. Linklater began with&nbsp;
just an initial outline and wrote each section&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.680
of the characters' lives along the way. The result&nbsp;
is an authentic, visceral depiction of growing up.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:34.560
The film follows Mason Evans, Jr. who at the&nbsp;
beginning of the film is just 6 years old.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.920
The plot follows Mason through&nbsp;
the next dozen years of his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.720
as he navigates family, romance and&nbsp;
everything else that comes with adolescence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.640
Ethan Hawke and Patricia Arquette co-star as&nbsp;
Mason's divorced parents, Mason Sr. and Olivia.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.880
The film received a ton of accolades,&nbsp;
including six Academy Award nominations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.960
and a Best Supporting Actress win for&nbsp;
Arquette. "Boyhood" received a massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.640
amount of praise from critics for the&nbsp;
beauty and remarkable nature of the movie.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.880
"You're kind of weird, you know that?"

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:07.840
"Is that a compliment?"

00:01:08.705 --> 00:01:09.447
"I don't know."

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.680
Barry Jenkins' "Moonlight"&nbsp;
holds a 96 score on Metacritic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.240
It is a film so good that it's hard to put&nbsp;
into words a description of its brilliance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.040
Not that that stopped critics from trying and&nbsp;
succeeding to explain just how mesmerizing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.680
film is, with various publications praising&nbsp;
its grand ambition and powerful message.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.280
The story follows a young&nbsp;
gay Black man named Chiron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.160
growing up in Miami through three distinct&nbsp;
periods of his life. It begins with Chiron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:41.280
as a kid, who is confused by his desires and&nbsp;
sexuality. It moves on to his teenage years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.720
as he begins to come into himself more and even&nbsp;
has his first sexual experience. It concludes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.520
with Chiron as a young adult, as he still&nbsp;
struggles deeply with accepting who he is.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.840
Each actor takes on the role of Chiron&nbsp;
in their own ways, with their own power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.680
while at the same time seamlessly&nbsp;
sharing the same character. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.920
Mahershala Ali's Oscar-winning turn&nbsp;
as the drug dealer Juan who becomes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.800
mentor and father figure to Chiron is&nbsp;
simply an unforgettable performance.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.240
"You got it all right now. Alright?"

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:18.560
Set in 1970s Mexico City, Alfonso Cuarón's&nbsp;
"Roma" follows a young woman named Cleo who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.680
works as a live-in maid for the middle-class&nbsp;
household of a couple named Sofia and Antonio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.560
their four children, and Sofia's mother. When&nbsp;
Cleo becomes pregnant, her boyfriend refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.680
acknowledge the baby. At the same time, Antonio&nbsp;
suddenly runs away with his young mistress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.480
As a result, Cleo finds herself bonding&nbsp;
more with Sofia and the rest of the family.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:43.760
"Roma" holds a Metacritic score of 96, with&nbsp;
many critics deeming it an intimate portrait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.160
and a grandiose piece of filmmaking. The&nbsp;
word masterpiece was thrown around by more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.440
than one outlet. Upon watching&nbsp;
"Roma," it's clear to see why.

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:00.240
Written and directed by Kenneth&nbsp;
Lonergan, "Manchester by the Sea"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.920
tells the story of Lee Chandler who,&nbsp;
after the death of his brother Joe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.600
learns that he has been made the&nbsp;
sole guardian of his nephew, Patrick.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.600
Upon returning to Manchester-by-the-Sea,&nbsp;
the fishing village where he's from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:17.440
to take care of Patrick, Lee is forced to face his&nbsp;
traumatic past and his estranged ex-wife Randi.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.480
The film was nominated for a huge string of&nbsp;
awards, including six Academy Award nods in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.920
almost all the major categories. Of the six,&nbsp;
Casey Affleck won for Best Actor and Lonergan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.480
won for Best Original Screenplay. Both wins&nbsp;
likely align with the experience the viewer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.440
has in watching the film: Lee's world is so&nbsp;
intricately constructed and Affleck takes on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.691
the role with keen skill. These achievements&nbsp;
are reflected in its 96 score on Metacritic.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:53.120
Based on the memoir "Twelve Years a Slave"&nbsp;
by Solomon Northup, this film adaptation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.400
Best Picture winner is a striking portrait of&nbsp;
a real man's horrific reality back in the years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.520
before the Civil War. Written for the screen&nbsp;
by John Ridley and directed by Steve McQueen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:09.040
"12 Years a Slave" tells the story of a free Black&nbsp;
man named Solomon living in upstate New York,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.920
where slavery is abolished. But when Solomon&nbsp;
is suddenly kidnapped, he gets sold back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:19.680
into slavery, facing the cruelty of not only his&nbsp;
circumstances but of a brutal master named Edwin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:24.080
After 12 years of this life, Solomon&nbsp;
finally has the opportunity to escape.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.880
Much of the film's praise&nbsp;
went directly to McQueen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.120
whose firm grasp on the subject and&nbsp;
presentation of this difficult storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.760
is thoughtful and memorable enough for&nbsp;
a 96 score on Metacritic. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.960
the cast members do phenomenal work, making the&nbsp;
deep authenticity of the film even more nuanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:46.400
and compelling. Chiwetel Ejiofor received an&nbsp;
Oscar nomination for his portrayal of Solomon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.480
while Lupita Nyong'o won the Best&nbsp;
Supporting Actress for her role as Patsey.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:51.780
"Cheers."

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.067
"Cheers."

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:58.800
Carrying a film essentially on your own is no&nbsp;
small feat for an actor. But with "Gravity,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:03.760
lead actor Sandra Bullock proves herself&nbsp;
more than capable. Directed and co-written&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:10.240
by Alfonso Cuarón, "Gravity" centers on medical&nbsp;
engineer Dr. Ryan Stone, as she begins her first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:15.360
in-space shuttle mission. Aided by veteran&nbsp;
astronaut Matt Kowalsky, their mission soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.160
goes disastrously wrong, putting them both in&nbsp;
imminent danger. With their shuttle destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:25.200
the two quickly realize they're stranded in the&nbsp;
middle of space, and Ryan is soon left on her own.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:29.840
Moviegoers who experienced "Gravity" were&nbsp;
likely not surprised when the film won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:35.440
seven of the 10 Academy Awards it was nominated&nbsp;
for. It's the kind of visually ambitious film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:40.560
that is bound to succeed in all of the technical&nbsp;
aspects, but the real impact of "Gravity" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:45.920
more than just a visual and auditory feat,&nbsp;
as evidenced by its Metacritic score of 96.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.880
It's clear to see what Cuarón's intention for&nbsp;
"Gravity" was: to fully immerse the viewer in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:56.000
the magical, if also terrifying, world&nbsp;
of deep space, right alongside Bullock.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:00.315
"Either way, whichever way, no harm, no foul."

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:05.280
"Parasite" became the first non-English language&nbsp;
film to ever win the Academy Award for Best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:10.800
Picture. However, even that groundbreaking feat&nbsp;
doesn't convey exactly how much of a triumph this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:16.320
film from director Bong Joon-ho really is. In&nbsp;
what has been called a career best for Joon-ho,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.480
"Parasite" will pull you in and surprise&nbsp;
you at every turn, even when you're sure you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:25.040
have a grasp on what's happening. This isn't&nbsp;
even to mention the ultra sharp commentary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:30.480
themes, and symbolism constantly at play&nbsp;
that landed this a 96 score on Metacritic.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:35.760
"Parasite" follows the struggling Kim family, who,&nbsp;
living in a semi-basement apartment, fold pizza&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:40.960
boxes for extra income to stay afloat. When the&nbsp;
Kims' son gets a job tutoring the daughter of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:46.480
wealthy Park family, the Kims scheme to all get&nbsp;
jobs in the Parks' affluent home. In a compelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:52.640
look into class inequality, greed and power, the&nbsp;
Kims' newly found comfort also becomes threatened.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.440
While "Parasite" is a film that's difficult to&nbsp;
fully sum up, many critics have tried to analyze&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.920
its different messages. It has been referred&nbsp;
to as uncomfortable and uneasy to watch, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:07.090
it ultimately presents a story that has something&nbsp;
important to say and holds true to many people.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.840
Written and directed by French filmmaker&nbsp;
Céline Sciamma, "Portrait of a Lady on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:17.280
Fire" offers a personal look into the intimacy&nbsp;
between two lovers in a visually stunning slow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:23.760
burn that earned a 95 score on Metacritic. Set&nbsp;
on an island off the coast of France in 1770,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.000
the story follows a young painter who is&nbsp;
commissioned to paint the wedding portrait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:33.440
of a rebellious soon-to-be bride. In the midst of&nbsp;
this assignment, they fall passionately in love.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.960
A beautiful love story deserves beautiful visual&nbsp;
imagery, which is exactly what director Sciamma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:43.840
and cinematographer Claire Mathon deliver.&nbsp;
The lead actors give excellent performances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:48.320
both individually and especially together.&nbsp;
Their chemistry leaps off the screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:53.124
and keeps you rooting for them even when you sense&nbsp;
that they only have a tragic ending ahead of them.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:56.800
Based on the novel "The Price&nbsp;
of Salt" by Patricia Highsmith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.200
"Carol" was adapted by Phyllis Nagy for&nbsp;
the screen and directed by Todd Haynes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:06.400
Set in 1950s Manhattan, "Carol" follows the&nbsp;
romantic relationship between a middle-aged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.480
woman in the midst of a messy divorce,&nbsp;
and a young aspiring photographer.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:15.360
Both Cate Blanchett and Rooney Mara excel&nbsp;
in depicting two characters whose outer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.760
lives have to differ from their inner feelings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.240
Getting to see their lives outside of each&nbsp;
other only makes their connection more palpable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:26.640
once they do come together. The film&nbsp;
received a 94 score on Metacritic with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:31.201
reviewers complimenting the chemistry of the&nbsp;
actors and the film's passionate love story.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.641
"And I thought perhaps you&nbsp;
might like to come with me."

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:42.400
Mark Zuckerberg is one of the most&nbsp;
famous entrepreneurs out there today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:46.960
and the 95-scoring "The Social Network"&nbsp;
offers a peek behind the curtain of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:52.000
man behind the news headlines. Written by&nbsp;
Aaron Sorkin and directed by David Fincher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.400
"The Social Network" begins when Zuckerberg&nbsp;
was still a student at Harvard. From there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.720
we see the creation of Facebook from its&nbsp;
roots and how it led to Zuckerberg landing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:05.600
on the receiving end of two major lawsuits&nbsp;
in relation to his growing social media site.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:09.600
As one of the oldest films on this list,&nbsp;
we can say that "The Social Network" has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:14.400
aged well since its release. Watching&nbsp;
it now, the observations seem more keen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.865
the writing just as sharp, and the depiction&nbsp;
of Zuckerberg all the more telling.

00:09:18.865 --> 00:09:21.440
"I know. I'm totally psyched about this too."

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.920
The only documentary on this list with&nbsp;
a Metacritic tally of 95, "I Am Not Your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:31.680
Negro" is a searing social critique based on the&nbsp;
unfinished manuscript "Remember This House" by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:37.760
James Baldwin. It is narrated by Samuel L. Jackson&nbsp;
and adapted for the screen by director Raoul Peck.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:42.160
Importantly, the film explores racism in&nbsp;
America through the lens of the deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:47.680
of three of Baldwin's close friends: Medgar&nbsp;
Evers, Malcolm X and Martin Luther King, Jr.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:52.160
In terms of documentaries, this one hits&nbsp;
all the marks of what a great one should be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:56.960
Beyond being a standout of its genre, it also&nbsp;
integrates the work of a literary great in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:02.719
Baldwin. Ever-timely and ever-fascinating, it's a&nbsp;
shining example of the power of the documentary.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:08.160
The attack on 9/11 is undoubtedly one of the&nbsp;
defining moments of recent history. It also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.640
led to the takedown of Osama bin Laden,&nbsp;
the leader of terrorist network Al-Qaeda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:17.280
after a decade-long search. The hunt and his&nbsp;
death are depicted in "Zero Dark Thirty,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:22.400
which was written by Mark Boal and directed by&nbsp;
Kathryn Bigelow. The film centers on fictional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:27.600
CIA intelligence analyst Maya Harris who&nbsp;
is in the process of finding bin Laden.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.320
Critics up and down the board&nbsp;
agreed that as a thriller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:35.280
it's a near perfect example of the genre. It&nbsp;
showed in its score as well, with "Zero Dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:40.800
Thirty" achieving an impressive Metacritic score&nbsp;
of 95. Beyond the compliments and glowing praise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:46.160
the film is also immersive and memorable, so&nbsp;
it's no wonder it earned its place on this list.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.191
"If you're right, the whole&nbsp;
world’s gonna want in on this."

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:56.240
"A Separation" is a beautiful piece of cinema&nbsp;
from Iran. Written and directed by Asghar Farhadi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:01.520
the film is about an estranged couple, Nader and&nbsp;
Simin, who are at odds with each other in regards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:07.760
to their marriage. Nader is refusing a separation,&nbsp;
resulting in Simin suing Nader for a divorce with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.400
the intention of pursuing a better life for their&nbsp;
daughter abroad. Further complicating things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:16.400
Nader finds himself in another court&nbsp;
battle when an abusive act against his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:22.400
father's pregnant caregiver, Razieh, ends in&nbsp;
a miscarriage and Razieh and her husband sue.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:27.280
The power of "A Separation" lies in the&nbsp;
compellingly complicated relationships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:31.760
of these two marriages and the ways in which&nbsp;
they intersect. While it's a character study&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:36.960
at its core, smart filmmaking brings a depth&nbsp;
to the film that makes it feel like much more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:40.720
Moreover, the writing articulates&nbsp;
its themes and messages flawlessly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:45.280
delivered through the actions of these nuanced&nbsp;
characters. With a Metacritic score of 95,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:51.916
it has the one key characteristic that arguably&nbsp;
each of the films on this list has: staying power.

